# Guide

@"@voxgig/apidef/model/guide.aontu"

@"base-guide.aontu"


# KNOWN ISSUE — three spurious entities, no supported fix yet.
#
# The Customs Window spec is Django-REST-Framework generated: each paginated
# list endpoint responds with an envelope component
# (PaginatedBulkUploadListList = { count, next, previous, results[] }) that the
# classifier promotes to an entity of its own. They carry no paths and no ops,
# so apidef warns "No paths defined for entity=..." and every target ships
# three empty entities (the 3 assertion-free "risky" tests in the PHP suite).
#
# Deactivating them does NOT work, and both obvious edits are traps:
#   - `guide: entity: <name>: active: false` parses (the guide schema has
#     `active?: boolean`) but apidef never propagates the guide's `active` into
#     `main.kit.entity.<name>.active` — the model still reads active:true.
#   - editing `.sdk/model/entity/<name>.aontu` is pointless: apidef rewrites
#     every entity file on each build.
# The real entities (BulkUpload/Party/Submission) already expose `list`, so the
# envelopes add nothing. Harmless but noisy; the fix belongs in apidef.
#
# This file SURVIVES a re-scaffold: create-sdkgen excludes the guide from its
# blanket overwrite and merges instead (it restores missing @-includes and
# otherwise leaves the file byte-identical), so customizations and notes kept
# here are durable across cedar-regen.sh. Requires the create-sdkgen
# guide-merge fix (in the local 0.16.4 tree; not yet published).



